# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  examples/server configuration — copy to .env and work top-down.
#
#  LEVEL 0 is enough to run the whole demo pair on BSC Testnet with zero keys
#  and zero gas on the server. The boot banner tells you which mode is active.
#
#    LEVEL 0  mode 1 — payer-funded (hash/transaction)      2 vars, no keys
#    LEVEL 1  mode 2 — + local permit2 settle               1 private key
#    LEVEL 2  mode 3 — b402 settle of EIP-3009 ($U)         b402 credentials
#    LEVEL 3  + /x402/premium — b402 permit2-exact route    2 more vars
#
#  Levels 0→1 STACK (mode 2 = mode 1 + permit2). LEVEL 2 does not stack: with
#  the B402_* credentials set the mppx route SWITCHES to mode 3 ($U /
#  `authorization` only — the TEST_USDT hash/permit2 paths are modes 1/2).
#  LEVEL 3 rides alongside mode 3 as a second, x402-wire route.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── LEVEL 0 · required (mode 1: payer-funded, BSC Testnet TEST_USDT) ────────
# The demo works end-to-end with JUST these two: buyers pay with `hash`
# (their wallet broadcasts) — the server holds no key and spends no gas.

# Receive payments at this address (your merchant EVM address).
# LEFT INTENTIONALLY BLANK — the server refuses to start until you put a
# real address here (a placeholder risks accepting payments to a burn
# address). Funds settle on-chain DIRECTLY to this address.
RECIPIENT_ADDRESS=

# HMAC secret for mppx challenge binding (mppx-managed mode).
# Treat like a JWT signing key. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
MPP_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional — BSC Testnet RPC override (the public default rate-limits).
RPC_URL=https://data-seed-prebsc-1-s1.binance.org:8545

# Optional — HTTP port. The client's vite proxy expects 3001 (its default).
# PORT=3001

# ── LEVEL 1 · optional (mode 2: + server-sponsored permit2) ─────────────────
# Set a settlement signer and the server ALSO accepts `permit2`: the buyer
# only signs typed data (no gas); this account broadcasts
# `permitWitnessTransferFrom` and pays the gas — fund it with tBNB:
# https://www.bnbchain.org/en/testnet-faucet
# NEVER reuse a mainnet key. Treat as a hot wallet: rotate, scope per-deploy.
# SETTLEMENT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── LEVEL 2 · optional (mode 3: b402 settles EIP-3009 $U) ───────────────────
# Set ALL FOUR B402_* credentials PLUS an explicit B402_CHAIN to switch
# settlement to the Binance b402
# facilitator: buyers sign an EIP-3009 `authorization` (zero gas, zero
# broadcast on their side) and b402 broadcasts + pays gas. Buyers are
# UNAFFECTED wire-wise (same mppx wire) — only the settle step changes
# (docs/adr/0002-settle-adapter.md). Credentials come from Binance OnchainPay
# merchant onboarding (no self-serve signup).
# RECIPIENT_ADDRESS above must be your b402 payout registered for the chain.
# The RSA key signs every b402 request; clientId + accessToken alone cannot.
# B402_BASE_URL=https://cb.binanceapi.com   # mainnet facilitator (pairs with B402_CHAIN=bsc);
#                                            # testnet: https://qacb.sdtaop.com
# B402_CLIENT_ID=
# B402_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# B402_PRIVATE_KEY=          # Base64 PKCS#8 DER / Base64-PEM / raw PEM (RSA key)
#
# REQUIRED with the credentials above — mode 3 refuses to boot without an
# explicit chain (a silent default would start a server whose settle step is
# known-broken):
#   B402_CHAIN=bsc           the verified-working eip3009 path, curated
#                            on-chain-verified $U (0xcE24…6666).
#                            ⚠️ MAINNET MOVES REAL FUNDS: mainnet credentials +
#                            a mainnet-registered payout, keep PRICE_DECIMAL
#                            small, fund the payer with real $U.
#   B402_CHAIN=bsc-testnet   ⚠️ authorization settles CURRENTLY FAIL here (the
#                            facilitator's eip3009 kind name mismatches every
#                            known testnet $U domain — docs/adr/0004 OQ2);
#                            only useful together with the LEVEL 3 x402 route,
#                            which DOES work on testnet.
# B402_CHAIN=bsc
# B402_RPC_URL=              # optional RPC for the mode-3 chain (falls back to the
#                            # curated default; the top-level RPC_URL above is
#                            # ONLY applied to mode 3 when B402_CHAIN=bsc-testnet)
# PRICE_DECIMAL=0.01         # per-request price in token units (default 1)

# ── LEVEL 3 · optional (+ /x402/premium: b402 permit2-exact) ────────────────
# Requires LEVEL 2 (the same b402 credentials sign these calls). Adds a second
# paid route on the PURE x402 wire (JSON 402 body + X-PAYMENT header) using
# Permit2 — the b402 path for tokens without a usable EIP-3009 door
# (docs/adr/0004-b402-permit2.md). Buyer pairing: the client's “x402 · Permit2”
# tab. X402_TOKEN_NAME must equal the b402 /supported kind's extra.name (the
# token's EIP-712 domain name, NOT its symbol). The server resolves the payment
# per request and shares one five-minute /supported cache across both b402
# paths. Its settlement-unknown recorder is in-memory for DEMO ONLY; replace it
# with durable encrypted storage + on-chain reconciliation in production.
#
# mainnet (B402_CHAIN=bsc, ⚠️ real funds):
# X402_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0xcE24439F2D9C6a2289F741120FE202248B666666   # mainnet $U
# X402_TOKEN_NAME="United Stables"
#
# testnet (B402_CHAIN=bsc-testnet, faucet-friendly — b402's testnet /supported
# lists permit2-exact for PancakeSwap TEST_USDT, so buyers can pay with
# faucet tokens):
# X402_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0x337610d27c682E347C9cD60BD4b3b107C9d34dDd   # TEST_USDT
# X402_TOKEN_NAME="USDT Token"
